hin single digits, or significant outside spending on either side, would warrant moving this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Stephanie Bice seeks a third term in Oklahoma's 5th District, a seat that leans Republican by about nine points, against Democrat Jena Nelson and two independents. Bice holds a decisive financial advantage, having raised roughly $2.4 million to Nelson's $740,000, and enters with the benefits of incumbency in a favorable midterm environment for her party.\n\nStill, the race has drawn more attention than expected: national Democrats have added it to their target list, and a September poll showed Nelson trailing by only five points. Expert raters remain skeptical, with most calling the district Solid or Safe Republican and prediction markets giving Nelson about a one-in-six chance. The forecast expects Bice to win by roughly nine points, with meaningful uncertainty given limited polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0816, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0827, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "202